,x.\n$$\n\nSince our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{v,w\\}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ In our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ v & w \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 14\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5d35991b-d925-5bca-a777-1935eac2dc98" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504730}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504727 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388974 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26b1ea4a-8431-5e9b-892f-bca7c95f80b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388976} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c9edc5-9c1a-5e2a-b1fe-0d7188e07e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388977} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d236a8-2a2f-599a-b81e-073c9d88e925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388978} {:answer/id #uuid "e60312e7-b230-5a43-aa7d-233414826603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388979} {:answer/id #uuid "82820516-f5de-5854-9a60-bb231ec12fc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388980}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388977} :answer-field/id #uuid "c310404e-e4a9-55ab-a9ab-4c596d9b583c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7f3f0d39-46aa-5c30-a041-815de875f218" :question/math-academy-id "q-158129" :question/problem "Verify whether the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we verify whether ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{18}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "71bec694-ee30-53a5-a601-06a5e14ae2ed"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504730 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388960 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "466a14af-419f-527e-b9f3-45ccda2c256a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388962} {:answer/id #uuid "49467b16-c66d-5981-95f1-f41a27d0f189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388963} {:answer/id #uuid "33